    "turn_text": "I am in my second term representing 35 cities and towns in Congress. They are stretching from the inner suburbs of Boston through the border of Rhode Island, cities like Fall River, Tonton, Attleboro, Newton, Brookline. And I have spent most of my life in Massachusetts, grew up in a family of medical professionals, but took a different path after I graduated from college, served in the Marine Corps for four years, deployed twice, came home, worked in the private sector, companies big and small for about five years, while also serving as a city counselor for my hometown. where I really focused on housing and transportation policy, and then ran for Congress in the middle of the pandemic in 2020.",
