  {
    "episode_id": 51087,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51087.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 6,
    "turn_text": "At the meta level, I actually am unpersuaded by micro narratives about Democrats' defeat based on different demographics or geographics or psychographics. You can look at the electoral data and then you can compel it to tell you a story about why young men, about why Hispanic men, about why college educated women, about why this or that county cost the election for Democrats. And the cold truth is Democrats really, almost across the board, lost vote share. The biggest city in my district is Fall River. It's a multi-ethnic working class city. And it voted Republican on Election Day for the first time since Calvin Coolidge. This is not a young man issue. This is sort of a Democratic party brand resonance with the electorate issue. Now, are there things that the party is doing wrong regarding young men? Absolutely. I think back to a quotation that Mike Pence had back when he was a radio host. Mike Pence was a very popular radio host in Indiana before he was a politician. And he used to say, I'm a conservative, but I'm not angry about it. And the analog for Democrats is, I'm a liberal, but I'm not condescending about it. I think Democrats have a problem with patronizing voters. and young men acutely feel that tone and gristle at it. And so we need to recruit them into a positive agenda rather than scolding them. And there are ways to do that, but I think are productive. I think we should have an agenda to build 1,000 tech bulk high schools in this country. I think we should in general have a agenda about building things in this country again. I think we should be significantly restraining the influence of social media corporations because their impairment of young men's sense of self in society has been very damaging for that generation. We're seeing young men retreat into themselves becoming less social and becoming less confident in important elements of real world experience. And these companies have no liability. They have no skin in the game for the well-being of their users. They're just productizing them.",
