    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51087.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 7,
    "turn_text": "You're saying the issue is being patronizing condescension, et cetera, et cetera. I definitely agree with that. I think I'd wonder, though, is the issue tone or is the issue the broader package of things? Because I think the pushback I could give if I'm going to put my Joe Biden stand hat on is Joe Biden's administration would say, well, we were the most pro-nuclear democratic administration of the modern era, even arguably by just any administration like Democratic or Republican. So, like, they would not have logged the thousand nuclear sites. They'd talk about how they were very friendly to vocational, vocational, technical education, et cetera, et cetera. So, if the sort of policy, if we just think of politics as a list of things, if we could pick out examples of what you're describing, being on the Biden agenda, but not translating, where's the gap there?",
