  {
    "episode_id": 51087,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51087.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 10,
    "turn_text": "section one. And ever since then, Democrats, I think took on too much of a crouch, too much of a defensive posture in talking about policy in-depth. And these attempts to meanify policy or to speak at it in high levels, I think, has not scrubbed. And particularly doing that only through cable news or only through press conferences. As you know better than most, Marshall, we are in a Balkanized media landscape where you've got to be willing to go everywhere, talk to everybody. podcasts, Twitch channels, town halls, mail. It's not sort of just New Age versus old media channels. It's just a kaleidoscope of all of it. And we've got to be hungry to do that. I got my certain politics by knocking 14,000 doors, having thousands of one-on-one conversations with builders. There's no shortcut to this. There's no magic headline. There's no one size fits all message. You just got to do the work. and we've got to be willing to do that work. We know that young voters, men, women are consuming huge amounts of content online, audio, video, text. Let's go meet them where they're at.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
