    "turn_text": "No, that's really smart. I think this gets at the whole Ken Democrats by the roger Rogan discourse. The thing that it misses, I'm not just saying this because I've been Austin so I come very much in the broader Joe Rogan cinematic universe at a podcasting perspective, but Joe Rogan talks about politics only like 10% of the time. The ratio goes up during election years, but it's Lots of bro stuff, bro history, bro hunting, bro comedy, et cetera, et cetera, et cetera. So I'll just kind of put you on the spot here and ask you this question. Let's say Joe Rogan, like, just says, hey, you know, Jake Ockencloss, you're a young person. I want to talk to young people in the party. What do you think about things? Like what are topics that you would be interested in talking about that wouldn't just be like, here's my like 10 page pitch or like my 10 talking point pitch for why you should vote Democratic. Like what are areas of your life that you think are relevant that once again could actually hit the chords that are existing in a relevant?",
