    "turn_text": "Yeah, and I just want to say is producer Marshall because my actual career started at PBS. I appreciate your answer because the worst version would have been, well, Marshall, turns out I'm super fascinated by YouTube comedy, like pretending to be so blunt. You're not inherently and that just doesn't work. You just gave actually a bunch of issues that once again are political, right? Like, you'll be having on the show in this case to talk about politics. He doesn't want you to do the comedy routine. But you gave just a bunch of issues and actually speak to interest areas he has. I want to start the fiscal responsibility one because it's actually really funny. I actually spend a lot of time watching those spaces. Those shows aren't my cup of tea, but at a narrative level, I'm super interested in what people are talking about. And just the like, why are we spending so much money narrative? really, really, really hits. Like, those guys are obsessed with that one. They're obsessed with the Pentagon failing audit after audit after audit. And I just don't see Democratic politicians being able to just come into that space and just speak to that just basic narrative reality, but just exist in a lot of people's heads.",
