  {
    "episode_id": 51087,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51087.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 23,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, and I think this is the really key thing here, which is, okay, so here's the push you question now. What I'm also really getting at, too, and this is where I think part of the populist vision on the left is incorrect, which is that I'd love for you just to talk about this from a perspective of being an elected official. I'm just like intuiting this by reading books and talking to people. on the podcast, but I just don't get the sense that top down economic populism of the Bernie style, Medicare for all, vast government expenditures, student debt relief, et cetera, et cetera, et cetera, motivates voters quite in the way that people think they do. And I think what's kind of happened here, and I've thought a lot about like, you know, there's this whole discourse about like Democrats lost Joe Rogan because Bernie used to go on Joe Rogan. Bernie used to convince Joe Rogan to be in favor of Medicare for all, but like I actually don't think that if you actually like sat Joe Rogan down and I did a post-op interview and said like what was really resonating with you about Medicare for like I get the sense that Joe Rogan really loved Bernie's like deeply aggressive 2015 anti-establishment thing and just policies like Medicare for all were just sort of Like attached to that, they were a way of like differentiating him from Hillary Clinton and Hillary Clinton's this like creature of the establishment. So this isn't to say that like, and I don't want people to think that I'm just saying like, oh, all left populism is like a bad idea and it doesn't work. But I'm talking purely is like a political project. But I don't think that you could just sort of take economic populism from a left perspective, sprinkle it over the swing states and just win, especially if the messenger is in 2015, Bernie going against Hillary Clinton. How do you think about this?",
