  {
    "episode_id": 51087,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51087.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 25,
    "turn_text": "So given this attack on middlemen, I be curious what you think about the big anti-trust debate that's opened up. And this is like a niche debate. This is like every single person in this debate has like a very direct stake. This isn't like blowing up the podcast circuit. But there's a lot of controversy over how Democrats are going to think about Lena Khan's tenure at the FTC like obviously there were a bunch and I like my wife works in venture capital like I work in tech like I don't want to people there are a lot of like center-left Democrats who are very unhappy of Lena Khan because they saw her as really tamping down on the tech industry and then you also had plenty of people to the right who are using like the Lena Khan thing as a sort of like see guys come in like the water's fine like come to the right Trump's gonna get rid of this but then you also have people to the left obviously who like putting the con, actually, there's plenty of centrist, like reasonable things, like the ban on non-competes, there's always different things we could say that were proven from the antitrust perspective, but how do you think about this big, how should Democrats think of antitrust moving forward?",
