  {
    "episode_id": 51087,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51087.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 27,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, and I think I'm glad you took it to the direction of health here, because once again, I'm dismissive of Medicare for all, not just because I have some disagreements with the policy, but that's just not on the table. If you look at the Senate, if you look at the overall legislative picture, there was just this moment where it seemed that the overtime window was open, and it's just not open. And I think that Democrats, and frankly, even Medicare for all interested Republicans of which they do actually exist, this is the realignment. I've talked to and covered those people. They need to find ways to talk about health care and the need to focus in that trust area that aren't just here is this big government program, we're gonna be able to pass because we have a legislative majority. So I'm just glad that you just listed off like five or six things that can be done, regardless of whether Democrats can take back to the Senate in the next few years.",
