    "turn_text": "I oftentimes, I'll meet with all the interns in my office, Marshall, and they're usually political science majors. And oftentimes, they want to go into policy or politics. And I will invariably tell them, read the political science books you're going to read. You've got to take economics classes. And what you really need to be able to do is look at any given issue and be able to draw a supply and demand graph and have an intuition about how is this policy going to move the supply chart or the demand chart? Because, and this goes back to our conversation about Obama versus Biden and their reactions to their recessions, ultimately policymakers can do both of those things. You can move supply graphs, so you can move demand graphs. Almost always,",
